        "location": "longterm-mem/internal/promote/page_scan.go:17",
        "claim": "pageSources is now only memorycard, so pages carrying `source: engram` (the store-agnostic key the reader accepted before this change) are no longer read at all. A memorycard memory whose lineage or mirror names an Engram observation with such a page is no longer detected as bridged, and a second page may be created for one piece of memory. Doctor's promoted-pages-eligible join (PageMemoryRef) also stops seeing those pages. The commit only argues that no page carries the legacy engram_*/memorycard_* keys. It does not show that no migrated page carries `source: engram`, which the old reader supported and the new tests now assert names no memory.",
