        "location": "longterm-mem/internal/promote/update.go:147-153",
        "claim": "entryFor no longer records PromotedRevision on any promotion path, but the field's comment in store.go still describes the revision as the evidence that separates an own unrecorded write from a human edit. After this change only `promote reconcile` sets it. Entries written by promotion therefore stay at revision 0, and Reconcile treats those pages as wedged and adopts them rather than refusing. This matches how card pages already behaved, but the reconcile_test fixture now has to set the revision by hand to keep the refusal path covered.",
